.TH fmt_escapechardoublequotedshell 3
.SH NAME
fmt_escapechardoublequotedshell \- escape characters for shell double-quotes
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
size_t \fBfmt_escapechardoublequotedshell\fR(char *\fIdest\fR, int \fIch\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfmt_escapechardoublequotedshell\fR escapes characters that have special meaning inside double-quoted strings in POSIX-compliant shells.
.PP
If \fIch\fR is one of '"', '$', '`', or '\\', it is escaped by prepending a backslash, resulting in a 2-byte sequence.
.PP
All other characters are copied to \fIdest\fR as a 1-byte sequence.
.PP
If \fIdest\fR is not NULL, the result is written to \fIdest\fR.
.PP
The function returns the number of bytes required (or written).
.SH SEE ALSO
fmt_escapecharc(3)